can be of the following two types:\n\n- When a system of equations has a *single* solution, it is called *consistent independent*.\n- When a system of equations has an *infinite number* of solutions, it is called *consistent dependent*.\n\nWe can summarize these definitions using the diagram shown below.\n\n![](images/16/1692fbea298339ff839cf2f14986d51af45d1ec72b2b7d0de179336bdef40c0e.png)\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution.\n\nFirst, we can solve the first equation for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x - 3y &= -9 \\\\ -2x &= -9 + 3y \\\\ x &= \\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=\\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation to obtain an equation that we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x - 3y &= -9 \\\\ -2\\left(\\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}y\\right) - 3y &= -9 \\\\ -9 + 3y - 3y &= -9 \\\\ -9 &= -9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the system is consistent dependent." 13194139536588 17592186045436 false] [17592186567832 1074 "A system of equations is *consistent* if it has at least one solution. Otherwise, it is called *inconsistent*.\n\nConsistent systems, in turn, can be of the following two types:\n\n- When a system of equations has a *single* solution, it is called *consistent independent*.\n- When a system of equations has an *infinite number* of solutions, it is called *consistent dependent*.\n\nWe can summarize these definitions using the diagram shown below.\n\n![](images/16/1692fbea298339ff839cf2f14986d51af45d1ec72b2b7d0de179336bdef40c0e.png)\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution.\n\nFirst, we can solve the first equation for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x - 3y &= -9 \\\\ -2x &= -9 + 3y \\\\ x &= \\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=\\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation to obtain an equation that we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x - 6y &= -18 \\\\ -4\\left(\\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}y\\right) - 6y &= -18 \\\\ -18 + 6y - 6y &= -18 \\\\ -18 &= -18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the system is consistent dependent." 13194139536588 17592186045436 true] [17592186574871 1168 "generators/da/da123f7ef3a3d73f56d896d4d39e06d5229fdcaa9ef0ad062cdd58627ff8f15b/generator.py" 13194139536588 17592186045436 true] [17592186574871 1169 #uuid "67f32c88-8486-5940-b96e-87ef88d4b32e" 13194139536588 17592186045436 true] [17592186574872 1168 "generators/72/7281c419e02d8b3024558ac1486300b59c7cbd92544845b110eb82dfa2a5dc4f/generator.py" 13194139536588 17592186045436 true] [17592186574872 1169 #uuid "3c913493-bb92-52ee-8a4c-f39ba65ce61b" 13194139536588 17592186045436 true]] :edb/tempids {"generator-17592186198347" 17592186574871 "generator-17592186198348" 17592186574872}}
